temic multisystem involvement", "Regular smoking history (potential malignancy risk factor)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Neoplastic Syndrome with Hyperglycemia and Cutaneous Features", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4344827586206895, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The combination of a subacute painful rash and multisystem involvement with smoking history provides moderate support for neoplastic syndrome as a paraneoplast…"], "evidence_against": ["Subacute presentation without direct malignancy evidence slightly weakens neoplastic syndrome as the primary explanation, but the branch remains viable."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Endocrine Disorder with Hyperglycemia and Dermatological Features", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.25, "posterior": 0.31034482758620685, "danger": 0.65, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Subacute presentation without direct malignancy evidence slightly weakens neoplastic syndrome as the primary explanation, but the branch remains viable."], "evidence_against": ["Classic hypercortisolism features are absent, providing strong evidence against this branch despite some supportive LR values."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Reactive Hyperglycemia with Multisystem Involvement", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.103, "danger": 0.45, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The extreme hyperglycemia suggests chronic pathophysiology (insulin resistance or beta cell failure), providing moderate evidence against reactive hyperglycemi…"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Autoimmune/Inflammatory Syndrome with Hyperglycemia", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.069, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Other Unspecified Multisystem Syndrome", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.083, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Glucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3258620689655171, "posterior": 0.3258620689655171, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Paraneoplastic Rash with Insulin Resistance from Solid Tumor", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1086206896551724, "posterior": 0.1086206896551724, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the painful erythematous rash with papules/plaques and subacute multisystem symptoms (fatigue, malaise, GI issues) strongly suggest a neoplastic process via paraneoplastic syndrome, given the pa…", "summary": "The combination of a subacute painful rash and multisystem involvement with smoking history provides moderate support for neoplastic syndrome as a paraneoplastic mechanism."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the combination of hyperglycemia and rash represent hypercortisolism (e.g., Cushing's syndrome), particularly given the absence of beta-cell destruction evidence and possible stress-induced fea…", "summary": "The absence of classic Cushing's features (moon face, buffalo hump) and normal temperature weakens this interpretation, but the LR+ for rash in endocrine disorders still provides weak support."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the acute gastrointestinal symptoms and multisystem involvement (fatigue, rash) represent physiologic stress leading to reactive hyperglycemia, as suggested by the RAG context on stress-induced hy…", "summary": "Acute stress could explain hyperglycemia, but the LR+ for reactive hyperglycemia is minimal, supporting this as a weak possibility."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the subacute 1-week course (vs chronic) and absence of direct malignancy findings inconsistent with a neoplastic syndrome explanation for the rash and hyperglycemia?", "summary": "Subacute presentation without direct malignancy evidence slightly weakens neoplastic syndrome as the primary explanation, but the branch remains viable."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the normal temperature (36.4°C) and lack of typical hypercortisolism features (moon face, buffalo hump) inconsistent with an endocrine disorder explanation for the rash and hyperglycemia?", "summary": "Classic hypercortisolism features are absent, providing strong evidence against this branch despite some supportive LR values."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the >500 mg/dL hyperglycemia more consistent with chronic hyperglycemia (e.g., insulin resistance or beta cell failure) than reactive hyperglycemia from acute systemic stress?", "summary": "The extreme hyperglycemia suggests chronic pathophysiology (insulin resistance or beta cell failure), providing moderate evidence against reactive hyperglycemia."}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "No branch meets posterior >= 0.75 for confirmation. B1.1 (alpha cell tumor) has posterior=0.326, and B2 (endocrine disorder) has posterior=0.310. Dangerous alternatives (B1) remain unresolved with posterior=0.434. Further discriminators (e.g., imaging for glucagonoma, tumor markers) are available to refine the differential."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.5, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.3258620689655171, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely underlying pathophysiology of this patient’s condition?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Alpha cell tumor"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Beta cell destruction"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Beta cell tumor"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Hypercortisolism"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Insulin resistance"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Postprandial hyperglycemia', 'Hyperglycemia', 'Hypertriglyceridemia'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.434}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "Glucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor)", "posterior": 0.326, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader